# Run once, in one process, before any test process starts. Blank lines and
# # comments ignored; everything else is executed by the module's interpreter
# with the module directory as the working directory.
#
# Building the track pool is the expensive part of importing `tracks`, and it is
# cached on disk (tracks/__pycache__/pool). The cache makes the *second* process
# cheap - but the runner starts N processes at once, so on a cold cache all N
# build the whole pool simultaneously and none of them benefits. On a 2-core CI
# runner that is most of why the parallel suite was no faster than the serial
# one. Doing it here costs one build, once, and every test process then starts
# warm.
import tracks
